cgtools
=======

Small tools for CGTK. Two are ported from GNOME 1 as plain CGTK
programs, with nothing of GNOME left in them, and one is written for
CGTK.

  cghex   a binary editor, from GHex 1.2.1
  cgcalc  a scientific and programmer's calculator, and a slide rule,
          from GCalc of gnome-utils 1.4.1.2
  cgrun   a box to start programs from

Each has a README of its own in its directory, with its copyright,
what it does and who wrote it.

Building
--------

It needs CGTK 1.4, and autoconf 2.71, automake 1.16 and gettext 0.19.6
or later to build from git. The git tree holds no generated files;
make them first:

  autoreconf -vif
  ./configure
  make
  make check
  make install

make check edits a file through cghex's document, with no window, and
looks at what it then holds; and has cgrun read the .desktop files in
tests/data, match names against them and start programs.

A release tarball comes with its configure script, and starts at
./configure.

Translations
------------

Each program keeps its own catalogues and text domain, in cghex/po,
cgcalc/po and cgrun/po, and installs them as cghex.mo, cgcalc.mo and
cgrun.mo. The strings new in the tools, and all of cgrun's, were
machine translated and have not been reviewed by native speakers.

History
-------

The notes that GHex and GCalc came with, as they were brought in, are
in history/, unchanged: GHex 1.1.4's, the version brought in before
the useful parts of 1.2.1 were taken into it, and those of GCalc from
gnome-utils 1.4.1.2.

Licence
-------

The tools are under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
(COPYING), as GHex and gnome-utils were.

The tools' icons were drawn for them, and are under the GPL with the
rest. Each is one picture, as cghex/icons/cghex.svg, with the sizes of
it and the XPM that render-icons.sh makes kept beside it.
